8","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-05-10T00:39:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T09:38:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in at least 4.2.2, 4.3, 4.4 and 4.5 dev3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Linux Mint 22 (Wilma) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 Ti (nvidia; 550.144.03) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-3770 CPU @ 3.40GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I have two players (CharacterBody2D) run into each other they jitter. This seems to be most noticeable with small sizes 20x20 square for instance.\n\nThey don't always jitter with the same intensity, if they hit with just the right timing it's very apparent. It will continue to jitter until one of the players stops trying to move in that direction.\n\nThis happens with multiple different kinds of CollisionShapes and happens in either Forward+ or Compability\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHave two players using CharacterBody2D run into each other, both using input from a player. \nUse a small CollisionShape, 20x20 for instance. \nMake sure your resolution/zoom is close enough to see the shapes properly.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[jitter_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20130944/jitter_bug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":